      "sandbox_host_not_switchable: the environment credential field is collected by the vault but this spec pins the LIVE host https://api.paddle.com. Paddle's sandbox is a different host (https://sandbox-api.paddle.com) with its own API keys, and spec v1 base_url has no conditional form (only a literal, {fromCredential} or a {template} over credential values), so an environment='sandbox' credential would still be sent to production. A sandbox user needs either a separate spec or a base_url mapping helper in spec v2.",
      "read_only_surface: all four tools are GET. Paddle's write surface (create/update product, price, customer, transaction, subscription operations) is deliberately excluded from this wave, so no tool carries write:true.",
      "per_page clamp max 200 follows Paddle's documented maximum page size; the default of 20 is a local choice to keep tool responses small, not Paddle's own default.",
      "rateLimit 30/min is a local courtesy and spend guard chosen here. Paddle publishes its own per-endpoint ceilings via the Rate-Limit response headers, which this spec does not read.",
      "pick sources follow the documented data[] plus meta.pagination envelope from the Paddle API reference, not a live 2xx: no account was held, so the proof below covers wiring only, never payload shape."
